            <ArticleTitle>Analgesic activity of dipipanone hydrochloride in student volunteers.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>97-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Dipipanone hydrochloride raised the threshold to ischaemic pain in healthy human volunteers. The lowest dose producing a significant rise in pain threshold was 10.0 mg. The peak effect for all doses was reached after about 2 hr. Side effects, the most common of which were drowsiness, nausea, and vertigo, are described and analysed. The drug was shown to be a histamine liberator and to cause pain and tenderness at injection sites.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
